WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.157 --> 00:00:01.650
(jazzy music)

00:00:05.661 --> 00:00:07.820
- [Voiceover] Salt's delicious as heck.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.256
It goes great on fries, chips, soups,

00:00:10.256 --> 00:00:12.056
and all kinds of savory items.

00:00:12.056 --> 00:00:13.612
But salt on desserts?

00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:15.018
You don't think about it.

00:00:15.018 --> 00:00:17.454
So why does salt work so, so, so well

00:00:17.454 --> 00:00:19.823
sprinkled on top of
chocolate chip cookies?

00:00:19.823 --> 00:00:21.481
Seriously, try it.

00:00:21.481 --> 00:00:23.132
Well, one reason it works so dang good

00:00:23.132 --> 00:00:25.999
is 'cause sugar tasty and salt is tasty.

00:00:25.999 --> 00:00:27.612
So you layer one good flavor on another,

00:00:27.612 --> 00:00:29.341
and you got a lot of
good business going on.

00:00:29.341 --> 00:00:30.433
Duh.

00:00:30.433 --> 00:00:32.150
But that's not the whole story.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.752
Salt is special because
it isn't just tasty,

00:00:34.752 --> 00:00:37.620
it has taste-enhancing qualities.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.618
What does that mean?

00:00:38.618 --> 00:00:41.591
Adults have hundreds of
thousands of taste receptor cells

00:00:41.591 --> 00:00:43.714
that live primarily on our tongues.

00:00:43.714 --> 00:00:45.538
Though they also live in the intestines.

00:00:45.538 --> 00:00:46.396
- [Voiceover] Gross.

00:00:46.396 --> 00:00:47.440
- [Voiceover] Some of these receptors

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.810
become activated when
we eat something sugary,

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:52.061
but if you add sodium in to the equation,

00:00:52.061 --> 00:00:54.022
some of these sweet receptors that don't

00:00:54.022 --> 00:00:57.053
normally activate when we
have just sugar, become alert.

00:00:57.053 --> 00:00:58.156
- [Voiceover] Oh shit.

00:00:58.156 --> 00:01:00.966
- [Voiceover] This intensifies the sugar.

00:01:00.966 --> 00:01:02.821
To get this double punch of sweetness,

00:01:02.821 --> 00:01:04.610
a pinch of salt is all you need.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:06.863
So get to pinching, cookie lovers.

00:01:06.863 --> 00:01:08.296
(jazzy music)

